  "body": "https://whatpr.org/html/3934/rendering.html#the-fieldset-and-legend-elements\r\n> Otherwise, behave as 'block'\\.\r\n\r\nBased on a prototype [implementation](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1483787) in Gecko, I don't see a problem with allowing the _rendered legend_ to use table layout.\r\n```html\r\n<fieldset>\r\n  <table style=\"-webkit-appearance: fieldset-legend\" border=1>\r\n    <td>cell1<td>cell2\r\n  </table>\r\n</fieldset>\r\n```\r\nrenders as:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4010828/44736831-94325680-aaf0-11e8-9926-ed9bc2152235.png)\r\n\r\nI think the spec could just say that the `display` value of a rendered legend _behaves as_ if its _computed value_ was blockified.",
